# Headers for anything Cloudflare's asset server answers directly.
#
# The Worker sets these too (see noFraming() in src/worker/index.ts), but it never sees most
# requests: a path that matches a static asset — "/", "/trust", "/request", "/reports", every
# file in dist — is served by the asset layer without invoking the Worker at all. Verified the
# hard way: after adding the header in the Worker, /watch carried it and / did not.
#
# frame-ancestors 'none' is the second half of the overlay embed policy in
# src/overlay-sanitize.ts. That side only permits a cross-origin https iframe, because a
# cross-origin frame cannot reach window.parent and therefore cannot read the content key out
# of a viewer's page. What it cannot prevent on its own is an allowed embed navigating ITSELF
# to e2emoq.com afterwards, which would make it same-origin. This makes that arrival
# render nothing. Both halves are required.
#
# Nothing here frames itself, so this costs no functionality.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
